§ `s 5 -- must I claim`

-- c064: the newborn upfront payment needs no claim (s 5(2)); FTB by instalment or for a past period does (s 5(1)).
#ASSERT `Must I make a claim to be paid this` `FTB by instalment`
#ASSERT `Must I make a claim to be paid this` `FTB for a past period`
#ASSERT NOT `Must I make a claim to be paid this` `the newborn upfront payment`

§ `ss 7, 7A, 8, 9 -- my instalment claim`

-- c064: Chloe claims 60 days before Oliver is due -- after the early claim day (97 days before), so effective.
#ASSERT `Is my claim for FTB by instalment effective` `Chloe's claim 60 days before Oliver is due`
#ASSERT `Is my claim for FTB by instalment effective` `a claim 97 days before the due date`
#ASSERT NOT `Is my claim for FTB by instalment effective` `a claim 120 days before the due date`
#ASSERT NOT `Is my claim for FTB by instalment effective` `a claim with no bank account and no promise of one`
#ASSERT NOT `Is my claim for FTB by instalment effective` `a claim without the partner's TFN statement`

-- s 15A: a promised bank account must be nominated within 28 days, or the claim is taken never to have been made.
#ASSERT NOT `Is my claim lost for want of bank details` TRUE TRUE 28
#ASSERT `Is my claim lost for want of bank details` TRUE TRUE 29

-- s 15B, c064: Oliver due 60 days after the claim, born on day 55: determined by day 55. Born late (day 100): by day 88.
#ASSERT `How many days until my early claim is determined` 60 55 EQUALS 55
#ASSERT `How many days until my early claim is determined` 60 100 EQUALS 88

§ `ss 10, 14A -- my lump-sum claim for a past period`

-- s 10(2), (2A): by the end of the next income year, or a further period allowed, but never past the second.
#ASSERT `By the end of which income year must I act` 2036 FALSE 0 EQUALS 2037
#ASSERT `By the end of which income year must I act` 2036 TRUE 2040 EQUALS 2038

#ASSERT `Is my claim for FTB for a past period effective` `Chloe's lump-sum claim for 2036 made in 2037`
#ASSERT NOT `Is my claim for FTB for a past period effective` `a lump-sum claim for 2036 made in 2038`
#ASSERT `Is my claim for FTB for a past period effective` `a lump-sum claim for 2036 made in 2038 with more time allowed`
#ASSERT NOT `Is my claim for FTB for a past period effective` `a lump-sum claim for 2036 made in 2039 with more time allowed`

-- s 14A: a claim in 2037 for 2035, with the return never lodged, or lodged in 2037 (after the end of 2036): never made.
-- A claim in 2037 for 2036 with the return lodged in 2037: fine. Not required to lodge: s 14A(2) does not bite.
#ASSERT `Is my lump-sum claim lost for a late tax return` 2035 2037 TRUE 0 FALSE 0
#ASSERT `Is my lump-sum claim lost for a late tax return` 2035 2037 TRUE 2037 FALSE 0
#ASSERT NOT `Is my lump-sum claim lost for a late tax return` 2036 2037 TRUE 2037 FALSE 0

§ `ss 20, 23 -- paid by instalment on my estimate`

-- s 20(1), (2), (2A): a reasonable estimate is used; an unreasonable one means no entitlement; else the notice's figure.
#ASSERT `What is my FTB worked out on` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `my own estimate`
#ASSERT `What is my FTB worked out on` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `nothing: I am not entitled while my estimate is not reasonable`

-- s 23(2): fortnightly unless the Secretary has determined weekly. c064: a daily rate of $7.75 (ASSUMED) for 14 days.
#ASSERT `How many days are in my instalment period` TRUE EQUALS 7

#ASSERT `How much is my FTB instalment` 7.75 14 EQUALS 108.50

§ `ss 31A(2), 31E -- revising my estimate during the year`

-- Days counted from 1 July (day 1). Estimate given on day 100; last paid instalment period ended day 114. An increase
-- runs from day 100; a decrease from day 115.
#ASSERT `From which day does my revised estimate take effect` TRUE 100 1 115 EQUALS 100
#ASSERT `From which day does my revised estimate take effect` FALSE 100 1 115 EQUALS 115

-- c07a (ASSUMED figures): Chloe and Liam raise their 2036 estimate on 1 January. Paid 1500.00 so far; on the new estimate
-- 1316.00. Step 3: 184.00, over 184 days left: 1.00 a day off the new daily rate of 7.76, so 6.76.
#ASSERT `What is my daily overpayment rate` 1500 1316 184 EQUALS 1

#ASSERT `What is my daily rate for the rest of the year` 7.76 1 EQUALS 6.76

§ `ss 32A-32P, 105A -- the FTB reconciliation conditions`

-- c07a: met when both Chloe's and Liam's 2036 returns, lodged by 30 June 2037, have been assessed (ss 32C, 32D).
-- A single parent on income support throughout who need not lodge: s 32P (end of year) AND s 32J (income notified).
#ASSERT `Have I satisfied the FTB reconciliation conditions` `Chloe and Liam's 2036 year, both assessed`
#ASSERT NOT `Have I satisfied the FTB reconciliation conditions` `Chloe and Liam's 2036 year, Liam not yet assessed`
#ASSERT NOT `Have I satisfied the FTB reconciliation conditions` `Chloe and Liam's 2036 year, Chloe's return late`
#ASSERT `Have I satisfied the FTB reconciliation conditions` `a single parent on income support throughout, income notified`
#ASSERT NOT `Have I satisfied the FTB reconciliation conditions` `a single parent on income support throughout, income not notified`

#ASSERT NOT `Are my FTB supplements included yet` FALSE

§ `ss 105, 105A, 71(2) -- what reconciliation gives or takes back`

-- c07a, Part A only, printed rates (see the generator note): paid 2832.40 on a $70,000 estimate, final income $100,000:
-- correct 2528.80, a debt of 303.60. Paid 2528.80 on a $100,000 estimate, final $70,000: 2832.40 + supplements 1200,
-- top-up 1503.60 (only 303.60 before the conditions are met). Estimate right at $70,000: the top-up is the 1200 supplements.
#ASSERT `What is the result of reconciling my FTB` 2832.40 2528.80 0 TRUE EQUALS `I owe a debt`
#ASSERT `What is the result of reconciling my FTB` 2528.80 2832.40 1200 TRUE EQUALS `a top-up is paid to me`
#ASSERT `What is the result of reconciling my FTB` 2832.40 2832.40 1200 FALSE EQUALS `no change`

#ASSERT `How much is my reconciliation top-up` 2528.80 2832.40 1200 TRUE EQUALS 1503.60
#ASSERT `How much is my reconciliation top-up` 2528.80 2832.40 1200 FALSE EQUALS 303.60
#ASSERT `How much is my reconciliation top-up` 2832.40 2832.40 1200 TRUE EQUALS 1200

#ASSERT `How much do I owe after reconciliation` 2832.40 2528.80 0 TRUE EQUALS 303.60

§ `ss 28, 28AA, 32AF -- unlodged returns and repeated nil years`

-- s 28: FTB for 2036 is cancelled in 2038 if a required return is still unlodged and unassessed; not yet in 2037.
-- c064/s 28AA: the newborn upfront payment goes with it if the supplement days are in that year.
#ASSERT `Do I lose my FTB for an unlodged return` 2036 2038 TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Do I lose my FTB for an unlodged return` 2036 2037 TRUE FALSE

#ASSERT `Do I also lose the newborn upfront payment` TRUE TRUE

#ASSERT `Am I barred from Part A on an estimate` TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Am I barred from Part A on an estimate` TRUE TRUE TRUE

§ `ss 77, 78, 78C, 78D, 93B -- my debt`

#ASSERT `On which day after the notice is my debt due`  EQUALS 28

-- c07a: Chloe still receives FTB instalments in 2037, so no interest charge accrues on the 303.60 (s 78D(1)(a)).
#ASSERT `Must I pay interest charge` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Must I pay interest charge` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE

-- s 78C: a base rate of 3.95% plus 7 points over 365 days is 0.03% a day.
#ASSERT `What is the interest charge rate for a day` 3.95 365 EQUALS 0.03

#ASSERT `Can my debt still be recovered` 20

§ `ss 97, 99 -- waiver`

-- c07a: 303.60 is not under the $250 small-debt amount (the figure just before 1 July 2026, used as an example).
#ASSERT NOT `Must my debt be waived as small` 303.60 250
#ASSERT `Must my debt be waived as small` 200 250

-- s 97: an administrative-error debt received in good faith is waived on hardship, or if raised after the end of the
-- next income year and 13 weeks from payment. Raised in 2037 for 2036 without hardship: not waived.
#ASSERT `Must the administrative error part be waived` TRUE TRUE TRUE 2036 2037 30
#ASSERT `Must the administrative error part be waived` TRUE TRUE FALSE 2036 2038 400
#ASSERT NOT `Must the administrative error part be waived` TRUE TRUE FALSE 2036 2037 400

§ `ss 108, 109D, 109E, 111A -- review`

-- c07a: Chloe cannot have her 2036 estimate-based decision reviewed until the year ends and both returns are assessed.
#ASSERT NOT `Can I ask for review of my estimate-based decision yet` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I ask for review of my estimate-based decision yet` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE

#ASSERT `How long do I have to ask for internal review` `a decision about my FTB by instalment` FALSE EQUALS `no time limit`
#ASSERT `How long do I have to ask for internal review` `a decision on my lump-sum claim for a past period` FALSE EQUALS `52 weeks after I am notified`
#ASSERT `How long do I have to ask for internal review` `a child care subsidy decision` FALSE EQUALS `90 days after I am notified`

#ASSERT `How long do I have to apply to the ART` `a decision raising a debt` EQUALS `no time limit`
#ASSERT `How long do I have to apply to the ART` `another FTB decision` EQUALS `90 days after I am notified`

-- s 109E: applied 60 weeks after notice of a decision whose period began in 2034, applying in 2037: paid from 2036
-- only (unless the reconciliation conditions were met). Within 52 weeks: from 2034.
#ASSERT `From which income year can increased FTB be paid` 60 2034 2037 FALSE EQUALS 2036
#ASSERT `From which income year can increased FTB be paid` 40 2034 2037 FALSE EQUALS 2034

